.TH CFOCONTROL.PY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-CFOControl t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
CFOControl.py \- run otsdaq FE macros over the MacroMaker UDP interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 CFOControl.py
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR HOST ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-refresh ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.br
.B python3 CFOControl.py
.B \-\-fe
.I FE_UID
.RB [ \-\-cmd
.I COMMAND
.RB [ \-\-inputs
.IR VALUE ...]]
.RB [ \-\-list\-inputs ]
.RB [ \-\-list\-outputs ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B CFOControl.py
is a one-shot client for the otsdaq MacroMaker supervisor's UDP
remote-control interface.
It is a Python port of the C++
.B ots_mm_udp_test
from otsdaq-utilities, with YAML configuration and IPv6 support added.
It sends one request, waits for the reply, prints it and exits.
.PP
The mode is chosen by which options are present:
.TP
.B "(no \-\-fe)"
Send
.B GetFrontendMacroInfo
and print every front-end UID the MacroMaker reports.
.TP
.BI \-\-fe " FE_UID"
Print every FE macro registered for that front-end, with its input and
output counts.
.TP
.BI \-\-fe " FE_UID " \-\-cmd " COMMAND " \-\-list\-inputs | \-\-list\-outputs
Print the input and/or output parameter names of one macro.
.TP
.BI \-\-fe " FE_UID " \-\-cmd " COMMAND"
Run the macro with the positional
.B \-\-inputs
values, then print each URI-decoded output as
.IR "name: value" .
.PP
.B This tool writes to production timing hardware.
For a CFO front-end the registered macros include
.BR "CFO Write" ,
.BR "CFO Halt" ,
.BR "CFO Hard Reset" ,
.B "Launch Runplan"
and
.BR "Shutdown Link Tx" .
There is no confirmation prompt, no dry-run mode, no allow-list and no
read-back.
The MacroMaker runs every UDP request as user
.B NO-USER
with permission
.BR "allUsers: 255" ,
so the server adds no protection either.
Confirm every write with a separate
.B "CFO Read"
on the same address.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
YAML configuration file; see
.BR config.yaml (5).
Without this option
.I config.yaml
in the script's own directory is read if it exists, otherwise built-in
defaults are used.
A named
.I FILE
that does not exist is fatal.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
IPv4 address, IPv6 address or hostname of the MacroMaker supervisor.
Overrides
.BR connection.host .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
UDP port of the MacroMaker.
Overrides
.BR connection.port .
A value of 0 is ignored.
.TP
.BR \-\-fe ", " \-\-frontend " \fIFE_UID\fR"
Front-end interface UID, for example
.BR CFO0 .
Must match exactly.
.TP
.BR \-\-cmd ", " \-\-command " \fICOMMAND\fR"
FE macro name, exactly as listed by
.BR "\-\-fe" ,
including spaces and case; quote it.
.TP
.BI \-\-inputs " VALUE ..."
Input values in parameter order.
The count must equal the macro's input count, or the command is not sent and
the expected parameter names are printed.
.B Known defect:
a macro with two or more inputs is mis-framed on the wire, so only the first
input reaches the macro (see BUGS).
.TP
.B \-\-list\-inputs
With
.B \-\-cmd
print the macro's input parameter names and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-outputs
With
.B \-\-cmd
print the macro's output parameter names and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Issue an extra
.B GetFrontendMacroInfo
before running.
The macro cache lives only in the process, so the first query is always fresh
and this option has no other effect.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print each datagram sent and the first 200 characters of each datagram
received.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.yaml
Default configuration, read from the directory containing
.IR CFOControl.py ,
not from the current directory.
.TP
.I ots_mm_udp_interface.py
Protocol library, imported from the same directory; see
.BR ots_mm_udp_interface (3).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B CFOControl.py
reads no environment variables.
.B CRS_PORT_MACROMAKER
is read only by
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-cfocontrol.sh (1),
which turns it into
.BR \-\-port .
Precedence is command line, then configuration file, then built-in defaults.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
Also returned when the reply is truncated (a warning is logged if the output
count is short) and when the MacroMaker answers with a plain-text
.B Error:
string, which is not recognised as an error.
.TP
.B 1
A
.B RuntimeError
from the protocol library (no reply within
.BR timeouts.first_packet ,
unknown front-end or macro, an XML
.B <Error>
element in the reply), an input-count mismatch, an empty front-end or macro
list, a missing
.B \-\-config
file, PyYAML not installed, or an uncaught
.B OSError
such as a host name that does not resolve (printed as a Python traceback).
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error, including
.B \-\-list\-inputs
or
.B \-\-list\-outputs
without
.BR \-\-cmd .
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl-C.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the front-ends known to a MacroMaker:
.PP
.RS
.nf
python3 CFOControl.py \-\-host mu2e\-cfo\-01 \-\-port 5000
.fi
.RE
.PP
List the macros of the CFO front-end, then the inputs of one macro:
.PP
.RS
.nf
python3 CFOControl.py \-\-host mu2e\-cfo\-01 \-\-fe CFO0
python3 CFOControl.py \-\-host mu2e\-cfo\-01 \-\-fe CFO0 \e
    \-\-cmd "CFO Read" \-\-list\-inputs
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read a CFO register (single input, framed correctly):
.PP
.RS
.nf
python3 CFOControl.py \-\-host mu2e\-cfo\-01 \-\-fe CFO0 \e
    \-\-cmd "CFO Read" \-\-inputs 0x9100
.fi
.RE
.PP
The module docstring's example
.B \-\-cmd """SetRegister"" \-\-inputs 0x9100 0x1"
names a macro that does not exist; its arguments are the reset bit of the CFO
Control Register.
Do not copy it.
.SH BUGS
Inputs after the first are sent in the output-names field because the input
string is joined with a raw
.B ;
inside a
.BR ; -separated
datagram, so
.B "CFO Write"
does not receive
.BR writeData .
A plain-text
.B "Error: ..."
reply exits 0.
A reply whose next datagram arrives more than
.B timeouts.next_packet
seconds late is truncated without error.
See
.I docs/ISSUES\-PENDING.md
(CFO\-001, CFO\-002, CFO\-004).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR config.yaml (5),
.BR ots_mm_udp_interface (3),
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-cfocontrol.sh (1),
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-cfocontrol.sh (1)
.PP
.I docs/INTERFACES.md
for the MacroMaker UDP wire protocol.
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
